  "details": "In the developr update today it was mentioned how... \n\n\"Some unnecessary options, such as “Mic Toggle” and “Close Menu” have been removed from the “Options” tab.\"\n\nBased on the comments there, it seems like a fair number of people are going to miss the mute button being removed from the tools menu. Many citing hand tracking controls being a key reason they used it, but I'm sure there's others too.\n\nI'm not someone who used that mute button myself, but perhaps a solution here could be to allow users to customise what features are included in 'Tools'? The menu to do this could presumably be located in the other customisation options for the radial menu.\n\nThis would also provide a means for users in general to add totally new shortcuts, such as toggling locomotion animations, or name-tags (two that I'd definitely use). Several things in the 'quick menu settings' would likely be viable as potential 'Tools' buttons. It would make the tools menu quite dynamic for each users personal needs, whilst also solving the loss of the mute button for those who are lamenting it's removal.",
